cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "apertus-eval-prep: reproducible LLM evaluation and release-readiness platform"
message: >-
  If you use this framework or the committed run artifacts, please cite the
  software. Note that the numbers in results/ are condition-specific and carry an
  evidence mode; they are not model rankings, safety certification, or production
  approval. See docs/METHODOLOGY.md#evidence-and-claim-boundaries.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhandari
    given-names: Shivani
repository-code: https://github.com/Shivani767/apertus-eval-prep
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - llm-evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - release-readiness
  - evaluation-variance
  - rag-evaluation
  - agent-evaluation
  - safety-evaluation
# No `doi` field: no archival deposit exists yet. Add one only after a real
# deposit (for example Zenodo) has been created, and verify it resolves before
# publishing a release. A placeholder DOI is a broken promise to citers.
abstract: >-
  A reproducible LLM evaluation and release-readiness platform that measures
  capability, variance, RAG and agent reliability, safety risk, latency, cost, and
  failure patterns under declared experimental conditions. It writes immutable
  run artifacts with pinned identity and machine-checked evidence modes, refuses to
  compare or aggregate runs whose dataset, task, prompt, or metric identity
  differs, and renders reports that preserve missing evidence as unavailable rather
  than zero. It supports offline deterministic CI, optional real open-weight model
  experiments, and human-review workflows. It does not certify model safety or
  production readiness.
